# This used to be a single `system_demo_toolchains()` macro call (see
# @prelude//toolchains/demo.bzl - "suitable for a quick demo or early
# prototyping... most real projects should copy/paste the implementation to
# configure them"). That's exactly what's happened here: the macro's full
# body is inlined below, unchanged, EXCEPT for the `cxx` toolchain's
# `archiver`/`compiler`/`cxx_compiler`, which need to be absolute paths
# rather than the defaults' bare "ar"/"clang"/"clang++".
#
# Why: several third-party crates' build.rs shell out to a C
# compiler/archiver themselves via the `cc` crate (ring, libsqlite3-sys,
# blake3, iana-time-zone-haiku - see third-party/fixups/*/fixups.toml).
# buck2 feeds those build scripts $CC/$CXX/$AR pointing at wrapper shims
# (@prelude//rust/tools/buildscript_run's __cc_shim.sh/__ar_shim.sh) that
# ultimately `os.execl()` the configured tool directly (see
# prelude//rust/tools/__from_any_dir__/from_any_dir.py) - unlike buck2's own
# native compile/link actions, `os.execl` does NOT search $PATH, so a bare
# "clang"/"ar" there fails with FileNotFoundError. Pointing `archiver`/
# `compiler`/`cxx_compiler` at this system's actual ar/clang/clang++ paths
# sidesteps that for both cases (buck2-native actions resolve an absolute
# path trivially too).
load("@prelude//android/tools:jdk_system_image.bzl", "jdk_system_image")
load("@prelude//tests:test_toolchain.bzl", "noop_test_toolchain")
